          "body": "This is a club story, not an Ireland one: London Irish, out of action since going into administration in June 2023, hope to return as early as next season under new owner Steve Daniels. Balls, the chief executive, says they would welcome a Championship place, England's second tier, at the earliest opportunity. The club previously explored joining the United Rugby Championship, a competition featuring teams from Ireland, but met resistance within the game."
