          "heading": "James Botham scores brace but Cardiff fall 36-21 to Sharks in URC",
          "body": "Wales back-row James Botham was the standout figure as Cardiff slipped to a 36-21 United Rugby Championship defeat to the Sharks on Friday. The 28-year-old scored a brace and, by Planet Rugby's account, emptied the tank on both sides of the ball, while Cardiff led 21-17 midway through the second half before fading in the final quarter. Sharks won despite losing captain Andre Esterhuizen to a foot injury after 52 seconds, with Ethan Hooker and Matt Romao among their try-scorers."
