          "heading": "Teddy Wilson earns maiden Wallabies call-up for spring Nations Championship Tests",
          "body": "Waratahs scrum-half Teddy Wilson is one of two uncapped players in Les Kiss's 33-man squad for the Northern Hemisphere leg, with prop Tom Lambert the other, Planet Rugby reports. Wilson is the son of David Wilson, who won 79 Tests and was part of the 1999 World Cup-winning side. \"I always want to make my family proud,\" he said. Ryan Lonergan has established himself as the standout No 9 in the squad."
