          "heading": "Shannon Frizell, Samisoni Taukei'aho and Tyrel Lomax ruled out of Europe tour",
          "body": "Three All Blacks are out of the European tour after the second Bledisloe Test in Sydney, according to SA Rugby Magazine. Shannon Frizell faces six weeks on the sidelines after rupturing the posterior cruciate ligament in his left knee, while hooker Samisoni Taukei'aho is expected to be out four to six weeks with a torn calf muscle. Prop Tyrel Lomax, battling a neck disc injury since Super Rugby, will stay in New Zealand for treatment. Richie Mo'unga, who missed both Bledisloe Tests, is not yet ruled out."
        },
        {
